  "body": "Found while working #882 (held branch `issue/882-adaptive-open-simplify` @ 70ac996f; see https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/882#issuecomment-6811353217).\n\n**What happens:** `adaptive/lift.rs` `lift_returns` keeps the microlifted plan only when its worst reading is not above the spiral's, and both are read in half-degree steps. On main, the 60 x 14 slot reads 48.0 against 48.0. Any geometry perturbation, even a 16 nm thinning of the opening, makes the spiral read 47.5, so the lifted plan is dropped and the slot falls from HSM (15.7 % load) to Offset rings.\n\n**Why it matters:** a plan choice that flips on a nanometre-scale input is a knife edge. It blocks #882's speedup (the bore goes from 115.6 s to 2.2 s) and any other change that perturbs the planner's geometry.\n\nDone means: the acceptance compares within a stated tolerance, not on equal half-degree steps. A pinning test shows the slot keeps the same plan under a perturbation of the opening's area in the 16 nm to 0.25 um range, and no adaptive fixture's verdict changes on main.\n\nPart of #882.\n",
